WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:01.099
Good morning John.

00:00:01.099 --> 00:00:04.870
This is a special bonus video not in response
to your last video but in response to my last

00:00:04.870 --> 00:00:07.470
video, because I said something that didn't
make any sense.

00:00:07.470 --> 00:00:11.910
I said that the majority of Muslims live in
Asia, not in the Middle East, and the reason

00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:17.070
why this doesn't make any sense is because
the majority of the Middle East is in fact

00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:18.070
in Asia.

00:00:18.070 --> 00:00:21.390
Now my point plays out, if you subtract the
population of the Middle East from the population

00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:25.020
of Asia, there're many more Muslims in Asia
than there are in the Middle East.

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:30.080
But the real problem with that statement is
that Asia is most people, like most of everyone

00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:32.240
lives in Asia, more than half of the world's
people.

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:36.859
And as I was thinking about this, what happened
in my head is the entire concept of a continent

00:00:36.859 --> 00:00:38.359
broke down and went away.

00:00:38.359 --> 00:00:41.710
So we are taught, in America anyway, I don't
know what everybody else is taught, that there

00:00:41.710 --> 00:00:42.800
are seven continents.

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:49.159
There's North America, South America, Europe,
Asia, Australia, Africa and Antarctica, the

00:00:49.159 --> 00:00:50.820
one everybody forgets 'cause nobody lives
there.

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:55.499
To the people who are currently on Antarctica,
I apologize for saying no one lives there

00:00:55.499 --> 00:00:56.499
but let's be honest.

00:00:56.499 --> 00:01:02.059
What a continent is is supposed to be any,
like, large contiguous area of land that is

00:01:02.059 --> 00:01:04.670
defined by ocean borders.

00:01:04.670 --> 00:01:09.280
This works fairly well for North and South
America and Africa, it kind of breaks down

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:12.880
everywhere else, in fact it kind of breaks
down for North and South America which are

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:16.659
indeed connected to each other, and for Africa
which is connected to Asia.

00:01:16.659 --> 00:01:20.770
And I guess it makes sense for Australia,
but is it just a really big island?

00:01:20.770 --> 00:01:22.649
Or is it a really tiny continent?

00:01:22.649 --> 00:01:23.649
I-unno.

00:01:23.649 --> 00:01:27.039
And then Antarctica, don't get me started,
it's an archipelago under the ice and the

00:01:27.039 --> 00:01:29.500
biggest island in the archipelago is smaller
than Australia.

00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:33.750
And then you've got the elephant in the room:
Europe and Asia, which are clearly by any

00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:36.530
geographical definition, the same continent.

00:01:36.530 --> 00:01:40.890
The only reason Europe is a separate continent
is because I was taught by people who are

00:01:40.890 --> 00:01:44.880
culturally European and they wanted it to
be.

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:51.030
But if there's any part of the definition
of a continent that is cultural, then there

00:01:51.030 --> 00:01:58.929
is no excuse for one continent containing
Russia and Indonesia and Japan and China and

00:01:58.929 --> 00:02:01.189
the Middle East and India and Pakistan...

00:02:01.189 --> 00:02:02.189
What!?

00:02:02.189 --> 00:02:06.899
Now this is exacerbated in my world by the
commonality of the Mercator Projection map

00:02:06.899 --> 00:02:11.190
which makes lots of things that are very big
look tiny.

00:02:11.190 --> 00:02:14.370
For example, last video, I was talking about
how the majority or Muslims lived in Indonesia

00:02:14.370 --> 00:02:19.730
and that just seemed impossible to me because
Indonesia, in my head, is very small.

00:02:19.730 --> 00:02:23.870
But then you drag it on up from the Mercator
projection and if it was in the same place

00:02:23.870 --> 00:02:26.050
as Europe, it's... it's huge!

00:02:26.050 --> 00:02:29.080
It stretches all the way from North Ireland
to fricking Kazakhstan!

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:35.230
Indonesia has the same land area as the UK,
Germany, France Spain, and Italy combined!

00:02:35.230 --> 00:02:36.250
So what's my solution?

00:02:36.250 --> 00:02:38.400
Do I think that Europe and Asia should be
one continent?

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:41.590
Or that Europe and Asia and Africa should
be one continent and North and South America

00:02:41.590 --> 00:02:45.040
should be one continent, and then maybe Australia
and Anarcarpartita?

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:47.310
No, not really.

00:02:47.310 --> 00:02:52.320
I think that continents are a useful idea
in grade school when you're introducing children

00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:56.700
to the idea that the rest of the world exists,
but for adult humans, I think that it's time

00:02:56.700 --> 00:03:02.130
that we move past this massive oversimplification
that leads to lifelong misunderstandings of

00:03:02.130 --> 00:03:06.460
reality and discard the entire concept of
the continent.

00:03:06.460 --> 00:03:10.510
John, you will see me tomorrow with my video
about the Global Goals which I am very excited

00:03:10.510 --> 00:03:12.120
to share.

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:15.540
Everybody go to globalgoals.org if you haven't
done that already, so you can study up a little

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:18.900
bit before that video, 'cause you're gonna
want to know.

00:03:18.900 --> 00:03:20.410
You're gonna want to know.

